**We do not recommend the September plan as approved.** Eighty thousand dollars of it, or 39%, is allocated to three channels that are not live, two of which have no GGMI performance history to size against. Committing that while applications are not funding and while the strongest channel is running below its approved budget is difficult to defend on the current evidence.

**We recommend a September figure of about $40,000 plus whatever the Azerion read supports**, composed of Bing at its full approved $30,000 and Quantcast at the monitored $10,379, with the Azerion line set once the full August vendor file is in. Native stays at zero. This funds the one channel with a proven cost per application to its approved weight, keeps a live audience, and defers $80,000 of untested commitment rather than cancelling it.

If the post-FOMC read shows demand turning, the deferred budget is available to deploy into channels that have by then demonstrated they can use it.

